{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/284363-using-a-tweaked-scion-system-for-a-campaign","id":284363,"title":"Using a tweaked Scion system for a campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-16T17:30:38-07:00","id":284363,"title":"Using a tweaked Scion system for a campaign","content":"My group and I are trying a tweaked version of the Scion system. Most notably, we're altering the impact of epics so that at higher levels a difference of one or two in an epic stat doesn't make an opponent impossible. <br /> <br /> For our run, we're saying Epics give their rating in bonus dice rather than bonus successes based on a scaling amount. <br /> <br /> So if we get to Legend 12 (or Ki 12 for this setting) and someone has Epic Dex 10, they will add 10 dice to their Dex rolls. <br /> <br /> We're sort of using the existing purviews and sort of making up others as we go. <br /> <br /> The setting is a dimension hopping setting. They first got taken from Earth by an orihalcum CD received as part of a limited edition &quot;Special Permissions Package&quot; with an MMO that represents the first world they were ported to. They've all become their characters (except the one person who's playing a native). <br /> <br /> The current setting is a sort of sci-fi Wu-Xia. We have a human swordsman. A vampire chick with nano-builder weapons (she's usually manifested chains do far). And we have two oni (one is the native). One is a big Tauren-esque space marine type with a massive axe. The other is a lithe type with more magic. <br /> <br /> The vampire race is more a Technorganic/cyborg race. The player wants to keep his character mostly flesh though. They are filled with little nano machines that allow them to adapt cybernetics easier (that's their race's favored purview). They were designed to fill the ghost/jiang shih race a la Chinese Ghost story. They evolved themselves this direction to better survive long, sub-light travels through space. <br /> <br /> The oni race are a branch of humanity that settled in the Flux, which we've described as being similar to the WH40k Warp, but not psychotic. It's more just chaotic without being malevolent. Most races in this setting use it to travel a la the Stargates in SG-1. The oni have lived in it forever so they're somewhat odd looking. The native oni thinks the displaced human turned oni is either from the deep or shallow part of the Flux (forget which the player decided on), because she acts a little strange. Talking about tutorials and quest givers and &quot;can I add you?&quot;<br /> <br /> There is also an imperial sorcerous race and a vaguely animal race but none chose to play them. <br /> <br /> The Ye Ren (Night People), Ren (People), and Yu (Jade) are Chinese based. <br /> <br /> The Oni are Japanese based. <br /> <br /> The animalish people, whose name I forget right now, are Korean based. (There's a Korean legend of a bear and a tiger that sought to be human. The bear lasted through the ordeal and was rewarded, the tiger gave up part way through. Then the bear ended up the woman who married the demigod said to have established Korea)<br /> <br /> <br /> We're also using a flat XP rate a la GMC. <br /> <br /> We'd earlier played basic scion with some changes (such as merging Monkey in the Middle) and making general purpose Boons cheaper to purchase. Otherwise we had a question of who would go for boons over knacks. We didn't change the cost of Specials or Pantheon purviews I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}